    28	
    29	Three paces away a man stood with the read open as far as it went, and Cael, who had a piece of that same read lying on every inch of his skin, could not feel him any more than he could feel the moon.
    30	
    31	By the end of the hour the not-feeling had a shape of its own. It was like standing in an empty yard calling a dog by its name, knowing the dog was somewhere close, and that it was his, and that it was not going to come.
