    40	
    41	"Every time," said Brom. "I can see you do it. You go still, and for a moment I think you've got it, and then I watch you get ready, the way you get ready on the floor before you go. It's the same every time. Your shoulders come down. Your eyes fix. Your breath goes short. You get organised, like a man about to throw something." He opened one hand. "You're aiming. It doesn't aim."
    42	
