   144	
   145	Cael looked up.
   146	
   147	"Everything else you've got, you point," said Brom. "The step goes where you send it. The thing in your arm goes into whatever you hit. The way you watch, the hooks and the columns, that's pointing too; you aim your whole self at a man and pull the truth out of him. You've learned every one of them by aiming." He shook his head, slowly. "You'll never aim this. Try to turn it into something you aim and all you'll get is a worse pair of eyes than the ones you've already got. And you'll never find out what it was."
   148	
   149	"What is it?"
