    78	
    79	Cael went in at three-quarter speed, high line, nothing committed — a question, not an attack. Brom let it come. Cael's forearm met his shoulder, and for the first sliver of the contact it was a shoulder, ordinary muscle over ordinary bone with ordinary give in it — and then it was not. The set arrived under his arm like a floor arriving under a dropped stone. And the force he'd put in came back out.
