   256	
   257	*Question worth tracking: is this a fourth thing developing, or is it the same underlying mechanism producing a new expression under new conditions? I don't have enough data yet. I have exactly one instance, which is not a pattern, only a data point worth watching for a second one.*
   258	
   259	*Fragment accounting from the bout, while it's fresh. Wind-adjacent: four bursts total, three read-fed and affordable, one reactive and expensive. Confirmed under the worst possible conditions that the fragment's cost structure is real — and learned its failure mode properly for the first time: it doesn't stop working when the legs go, it stops being worth using, which is more dangerous, because habit keeps reaching for it. Pressure-adjacent: zero deployments, by rule, against an opponent built to profit from every one. The rule held. Refusing it mid-fight has a cost of its own — attention, mostly — that I hadn't priced in. Price that in next time. Every ability has two ledgers: what it costs to use, and what it costs to carry without using. I only knew about the first one until tonight.*
