    21	His family held land at Velmere — not vast, but old, the kind of holding that had produced three generations of practitioners whose Kindlings had, without exception, resolved to Gold-tier or close enough to it that the family had stopped bothering to imagine a different outcome. His grandmother had been Gold. His mother had been Gold, barely, a hair's breadth from Silver by the numbers but Gold on the classification that mattered to the family's standing. His older sister, two years into her own guild placement, was already being discussed as a candidate for regional advancement.
    22	
