    24	
    25	"And then there's me," Brom said, without any weight on the sentence, the way you'd report a measurement rather than a wound. "Iron Skin Path. Copper-tier. My family expected Gold. Iron Skin at Copper is the kind of result that ends conversations at dinner — not because anyone says anything cruel, you understand. Nobody in my family says anything cruel. They just go quiet, and reschedule, and start talking about training intensification in a tone that makes it very clear what they actually think happened."
