editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-29.md:167:*IRON-ADJACENT.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-29.md:169:*What it is: the edge of B.'s read. A thin thing on the skin, all over, outside. It doesn't go out. Things come in.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-29.md:171:*Source: B. Third morning, mid-reset, not asked for. Ruling: same road as the other two. Close, and long, and a real person, and not taken. Found afterward.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-29.md:179:*Open questions: Two people in a room. A crowd. Somebody who isn't kindled. Whether it gets cheaper, like his. Whether it ever runs while I move. What it's for, if it isn't for anything I point. B.: it's for knowing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-29.md:203:*L., through the wall. Didn't.*
